   "text": "I read this as a PROTAC-type molecule with a VHL-binding end, a hexyl linker, and an aminopyridazine (hydroxyphenyl) end. I wrote it in sections, left to right.\n\n- **VHL end:** a 1-fluorocyclopropane carboxamide on the tert-leucine nitrogen. Its carbonyl links to a 4-hydroxyproline. The proline carboxamide goes through NH\u2013CH2 to a benzene ring bearing a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl group and an ether oxygen.\n- **Linker:** the O\u2013(CH2)6\u2013N chain runs from the benzene to a piperidine nitrogen. I counted six carbons by tracing the vertices of the drawn chain.\n- **Middle:** the piperidine C4 is attached to C5 of a pyrimidine. Pyrimidine C2 is attached to N8 of a 3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane.\n- **Far end:** N3 of the bicycle is attached to C4 of a pyridazine. That pyridazine carries NH2 at C3 and a 2-hydroxyphenyl at C6.\n\nFor stereochemistry, I took the tert-leucine and hydroxyproline centres to have the usual VHL-ligand configuration (S at tert-leucine; the 4-hydroxyproline as in the common VHL ligand). I assigned @/@@ from that convention and the wedges and hashes shown, adjusting the tert-leucine tag for my atom ordering. The bicyclic bridgeheads are drawn with plain bonds, so they get no stereo marks.\n\nSMILES: FC1(CC1)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N1C[C@H](O)C[C@H]1C(=O)NCc1ccc(cc1OCCCCCCN1CCC(CC1)c1cnc(nc1)N1C2CCC1CN(C2)c1cc(nnc1N)-c1ccccc1O)-c1scnc1C"
  }
